<mxCell id="c204" value="External (Laravel users — the ONLY external table this module references)" style="text;html=1;fontSize=12;fontColor=#12181F;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="72" y="1297" width="900" height="24" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
<mxCell id="c205" value="FK* = references public.users(id) — the only cross-schema reference anywhere in this module (§5, same zero-hard-dependency posture as WNE). sched_items.subject_type/subject_id is the same platform-wide polymorphic pointer, informational only, never a real FK — a vertical module (e.g. a Legal case deadline) links in this way without Schedule knowing anything about it. A table-level CHECK enforces the type-appropriate field shape: a task has due_at and no start/end window; an event has a start/end window and no due_at. sched_calendar_feeds.user_id/resource_id are mutually exclusive (a feed is per-user OR per-resource, never both/neither) — enforced by a CHECK, not application logic alone. Recurrence is expanded on read for the visible date range from recurrence_rule + sched_recurrence_exceptions — never pre-materialized into rows." style="text;html=1;fontSize=11;fontColor=#4A5563;align=left;fontStyle=2;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="40" y="1346" width="1500" height="70" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
</mxfile>
